In Material 3, contrast compliance in dark themes is solved systematically through the **M3 Tonal Palette architecture** rather than reusing identical brand hex codes across light and dark modes.

Here is the exact strategy we use to guarantee WCAG AA (4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text/UI components):

---

### 1. M3 Tonal Palette Shift (Tones 40 vs. 80)
* **Light Theme:** Brand primary is mapped to **Tone 40** (darker tone) to contrast against light surfaces (Tone 90–100).
* **Dark Theme:** Brand primary shifts to **Tone 80** (a lighter, desaturated tint of the same hue/chroma) so it achieves $\ge 4.5:1$ contrast against dark surfaces (`--md-sys-color-surface`, Tone 6–10).

```scss
/* Theme token definition example */
:root {
  /* Light Theme (Primary = Tone 40, Surface = Tone 98) */
  --md-sys-color-primary: hsl(var(--brand-hue), var(--brand-chroma), 40%);
  --md-sys-color-on-primary: #ffffff;
  --md-sys-color-surface: hsl(var(--brand-hue), 8%, 98%);
  --md-sys-color-on-surface: hsl(var(--brand-hue), 8%, 10%);
}

[data-theme="dark"], .theme-dark {
  /* Dark Theme (Primary shifts to Tone 80, Surface = Tone 6) */
  --md-sys-color-primary: hsl(var(--brand-hue), var(--brand-chroma), 80%);
  --md-sys-color-on-primary: hsl(var(--brand-hue), var(--brand-chroma), 20%);
  --md-sys-color-surface: hsl(var(--brand-hue), 6%, 6%);
  --md-sys-color-on-surface: hsl(var(--brand-hue), 8%, 90%);
}
```

---

### 2. Semantic Token Usage Rules
To avoid low-luminance text traps:
1. **Never use `--md-sys-color-primary` directly for body text** on dark backgrounds. Use `--md-sys-color-on-surface` (Tone 90) or `--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant` (Tone 80).
2. **Text inside filled primary elements:** Always use `--md-sys-color-on-primary` (which is Tone 20 in dark mode, providing $\ge 7:1$ contrast against Tone 80).
3. **Container Elements:** Use `--md-sys-color-primary-container` (Tone 30) paired strictly with `--md-sys-color-on-primary-container` (Tone 90).

---

### 3. Updates to Track Spec & Plan

I will update `spec.md` and `plan.md` to explicitly encode this contrast policy and automated verification:

#### Updated `conductor/tracks/user-settings-view-m3/spec.md` additions:
> - **Accessibility & Contrast:** 
>   - All text and interactive elements must satisfy WCAG 2.1 AA ($\ge 4.5:1$ contrast ratio for normal text, $\ge 3:1$ for large text/icons).
>   - Dark theme uses Tone 80 primaries and Tone 90 on-surface text tokens.
>   - Hardcoded brand luminance overrides must not be used without passing automated axe contrast audits.

#### Updated `conductor/tracks/user-settings-view-m3/plan.md` additions:
> - **Task 1.2:** Add `axe-core` / `@axe-core/react` contrast assertions to unit/component test harness for both theme variants.
> - **Task 3.1:** Run automated WCAG AA color-contrast scan across all component states in light and dark modes.

---

Would you like to proceed with this approach and begin **Phase 1: Token Mapping & Test Harness Preparation**?

