Here is the update for `UserDropdownMenu.tsx` to resolve the overlay collision and improve accessibility:

### Summary of Changes
1. **Z-Index Layering**: Set `z-index: 1050` on the dropdown menu container/overlay to avoid collision with surrounding elements.
2. **Accessibility**: Added `aria-label="User Profile Menu"` to the menu toggle button.

---

### Code Changes

```tsx
// UserDropdownMenu.tsx

import React, { useState } from 'react';

interface UserDropdownMenuProps {
  // ... props
}

export const UserDropdownMenu: React.FC<UserDropdownMenuProps> = ({ ...props }) => {
  const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false);

  return (
    <div className="relative inline-block text-left">
      {/* Toggle Button */}
      <button
        type="button"
        aria-label="User Profile Menu"
        aria-haspopup="true"
        aria-expanded={isOpen}
        onClick={() => setIsOpen((prev) => !prev)}
        className="inline-flex justify-center items-center p-2 rounded-md focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-offset-2"
      >
        {/* Toggle Icon / User Avatar */}
        <span className="sr-only">Open user menu</span>
        {/* ... user avatar / icon ... */}
      </button>

      {/* Dropdown Menu Container */}
      {isOpen && (
        <div
          role="menu"
          aria-orientation="vertical"
          style={{ zIndex: 1050 }}
          className="absolute right-0 mt-2 w-56 rounded-md shadow-lg bg-white ring-1 ring-black ring-opacity-5 focus:outline-none z-[1050]"
        >
          <div className="py-1">
            {/* Dropdown items */}
          </div>
        </div>
      )}
    </div>
  );
};

export default UserDropdownMenu;
```

---

### Verification
- **Visual Stacking**: Verify the dropdown appears above modals/navigation bars with lower z-indices (< 1050).
- **Accessibility**: Verify screen readers announce `"User Profile Menu"` when focused on the toggle button.

